+# Gradle daemon JVM criteria (Gradle 8.8+): run the daemon on JDK 21.
+#
+# Why: Flutter stable moved to 3.50.0, whose Android template uses AGP 9. Its
+# lint tool crashes under JDK 17 (the CI pins Temurin 17) with
+# NoSuchMethodError 'java.util.List.removeLast()' - List.removeLast() only
+# exists from Java 21 - while analyzing plugin Java sources, and lintVital
+# treats that as fatal, so the release APK could not build (a debug APK is NOT
+# acceptable). Asking Gradle for a JDK 21 daemon fixes the lint tool; GitHub's
+# ubuntu-24.04 runners ship Temurin 21 (Gradle finds it in /usr/lib/jvm).
+# This file survives the CI's `flutter create` scaffolding because create only
+# writes files that do not exist yet.
+toolchainVersion=21
